            <ArticleTitle>[SUNCT syndrome (short-lasting unilateral neuralgiform headache with conjuntival injection and tearing): a rare case in a paediatric patient with favourable response to topiramate].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>SUNCT Syndrome (short-lasting unilateral neuralgiform headache with conjuntival injection and tearing) combines neuralgic, migraineus and autonomic headaches, three of four primary ones described in the International Classification of the IHS (International Headache Society). This work describes a paediatric case evaluated under MIDAS score in which a new therapeutic approach with topiramate (TPM) was used.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
